  "goodToKnow": "Die Gedenkstätte is a memorial site, a central part of German Erinnerungskultur (culture of remembrance): KZ-Gedenkstätten at Dachau, Buchenwald and Sachsenhausen, the Gedenkstätte Berliner Mauer, and the former Stasi prison at Hohenschönhausen. Many school classes visit one. Gedenken means to commemorate, and der Gedenktag is a day of remembrance, like 27 January. Die Stätte is a formal word for place. Plural: die Gedenkstätten."
